From: archpower
Date: 2026-06-30
Subject: [PATCH] radeon: force MaxReadReq=128 on PPC64 for U4 compatibility

The PowerMac G5 U4 CPC945 x16 PCIe slot does not handle 512-byte
MaxReadReq from TeraScale (r600+) AMD GPUs correctly.  The GPU's
Command Processor issues PCIe Memory Read transactions at the
MaxReadReq size to fetch ring buffer entries from system RAM, and
these completions are mishandled by the U4 bridge, causing:

  radeon: ring 0 test failed

The known-working GeForce 6600 in the same slot uses MaxReadReq=128.
Forcing 128 bytes on PPC64 resolves the ring test failure.

Signed-off-by: archpower
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/evergreen.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/evergreen.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/evergreen.c
index 2d87f9b3177e..605a7ded9927 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/evergreen.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/evergreen.c
@@ -1277,16 +1277,24 @@
 
 void evergreen_fix_pci_max_read_req_size(struct radeon_device *rdev)
 {
-	int readrq;
+	int readrq = pcie_get_readrq(rdev->pdev);
 	u16 v;
 
-	readrq = pcie_get_readrq(rdev->pdev);
+#ifdef CONFIG_PPC64
+	/* The PowerMac G5 U4 CPC945 x16 PCIe slot cannot handle 512-byte
+	 * MaxReadReq from r600+ GPUs.  PCIe Memory Read requests at that
+	 * size cause completion timeouts that manifest as ring test
+	 * failures.  Match the known-good GeForce 6600 config (128). */
+	if (readrq > 128)
+		pcie_set_readrq(rdev->pdev, 128);
+#else
 	v = ffs(readrq) - 8;
 	/* if bios or OS sets MAX_READ_REQUEST_SIZE to an invalid value, fix it
 	 * to avoid hangs or perfomance issues
 	 */
 	if ((v == 0) || (v == 6) || (v == 7))
 		pcie_set_readrq(rdev->pdev, 512);
+#endif
 }
 
 void dce4_program_fmt(struct drm_encoder *encoder)
